---
// Fig. for "Schwartz-Zippel Lemma": putting real numbers on the bound —
// degree 2, checked over a field the size real ZK systems use
// (~2^254 elements), the false-match chance collapses to something
// smaller than picking one atom out of the universe.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 680 210" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <text x="340" y="34" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="14.5" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">our example: degree 2, over a huge ZK field</text>

  <text x="340" y="88" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="26" font-weight="800" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">chance of a false match &#8776; 2 / 2<tspan dy="-11" font-size="60%">254</tspan></text>

  <rect x="20" y="124" width="640" height="64" rx="8" fill="#121c2c" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1.5" />
  <text x="340" y="150" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="15" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">smaller than the odds of picking one atom</text>
  <text x="340" y="172" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="15" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">out of the entire universe</text>
</svg>
